{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-blog-post-js","path":"/blog/2010-03-23-expression-blend-visual-states/","result":{"data":{"markdownRemark":{"html":"<p>A few people have asked me what's the easiest way of doing transitions on Silverlight.</p>\n<p>One of the easiest ways has to be to use the VisualStateManager with Expression Blend, see screenshot for sample logged in state.<br>\nIf you don't know how to use this tool then start watching a few vids!</p>\n<p>To change between states you can use this code...</p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"csharp\"><pre style=\"counter-reset: linenumber NaN\" class=\"language-csharp line-numbers\"><code class=\"language-csharp\"><span class=\"token keyword\">if</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>WebContext<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>Current<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>User<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>IsAuthenticated<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n    VisualStateManager<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">GoToState</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token keyword\">this</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>WebContext<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>Current<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>Authentication <span class=\"token keyword\">is</span> <span class=\"token class-name\">WindowsAuthentication</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">?</span> <span class=\"token string\">\"windowsAuth\"</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">\"LoggedIn\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token boolean\">true</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">else</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n    VisualStateManager<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">GoToState</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token keyword\">this</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token string\">\"LoggedOut\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token boolean\">true</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span></code><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"line-numbers-rows\" style=\"white-space: normal; width: auto; left: 0;\"><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></pre></div>\n<p><img src=\"/images/blog/2010/3/sitedocs.jpg\" alt=\"\"></p>","timeToRead":1,"excerpt":"A few people have asked me what's the easiest way of doing transitions on Silverlight. One of the easiest ways has to be to use the VisualStateManager with Expression Blend, see screenshot for sample…","frontmatter":{"title":"Expression Blend visual states","date":"23 March 2010","category":"XAML & Desktop","tags":["expression blend","silverlight"],"image":null}}},"pageContext":{"slug":"/blog/2010-03-23-expression-blend-visual-states/"}},"staticQueryHashes":["764694655"],"slicesMap":{}}